From 734d0dc4665240ca3495adafe6f8645b150f2ac7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 22:19:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/23] fp8 : close the decode gap to Q8_0 (tg64 72 -> 89)

- mul_mat_fp8_gemv: defer the warp reduce to the end (fold per-block
  scales into the lane partial), 4 k-blocks per iteration for load ILP;
  bandwidth 445 -> 496 GB/s
- skip the n_pad zero-fill for the GEMV path (n <= 16): the padded
  tokens are never read, removes 450 cudaMemset launches per decode step
- convert: --fp8-output-weight writes an fp8 output.weight copy of
  token_embd (128x128 blocks, d = BF16(amax/448)) so lm_head runs on the
  fp8 GEMV; token_embd stays BF16 for the input embedding lookup

Measured (same box/day): tg64 72.03 -> 89.13 (Q8_0: 90.92), pp512
unchanged ~5914. Generation matches; PPL 6.2572 vs 6.2508 (no-ow) and
6.2464 (Q8_0), all within error bars.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet
